@startuml auth-sequence
!include theme.iuml
title teamscale-mcp — credential flow

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

actor "Deployer\n(env vars)" as Deployer
actor "MCP client\n(Claude Code, …)" as Client

box "teamscale-mcp (this repo)" $ws_bg
    participant "TokenCapture\nMiddleware\n(ASGI)" as MW
    participant "FastMCP\n(OpenAPI-derived tools)" as MCP
    participant "httpx client\n+ TeamscaleBasicAuth" as HTTP
end box

box "Teamscale server" $ts_bg
    participant "Teamscale\nREST API" as TS
end box

== Tier 1: bootstrap credentials (startup only) ==
Deployer -[$cli_color,bold]> MCP : <b>TEAMSCALE_SPEC_USER + TEAMSCALE_SPEC_TOKEN</b>\n(process env)
activate MCP
MCP -[$cli_color,bold]> TS : GET /openapi.json\n<b>Basic base64(SPEC_USER : SPEC_TOKEN)</b>
activate TS
TS --> MCP : OpenAPI spec (JSON)
deactivate TS
deactivate MCP
note over Deployer, TS : Bootstrap creds are used <b>once</b>, only to download the spec.\nThey are <b>never</b> used for a tool call made on behalf of a client.

== Tier 2: per-request client identity ==

group Missing identity headers → rejected before any tool
    Client -[$drop_color,bold]> MW : POST /mcp\n(no X-Teamscale-User / -Token)
    MW -[$drop_color,bold]> Client : <b>401</b>\n{"error":"missing …-User/…-Token header"}
end

group Authenticated tool call
    Client -[$tool_color,bold]> MW : POST /mcp\n<b>X-Teamscale-User + X-Teamscale-Token</b>\n(tool call, e.g. getFindings)
    activate MW
    MW -> MW : stash user + token\nin contextvars
    MW -> MCP : forward ASGI request
    activate MCP
    MCP -> HTTP : invoke mapped REST operation
    activate HTTP
    HTTP -> HTTP : read user + token\nfrom contextvars
    HTTP -[$tool_color,bold]> TS : HTTP <op> /api/…\n<b>Authorization: Basic base64(user:token)</b>
    activate TS
    TS -> TS : validate credentials
    TS --> HTTP : JSON response\n(client's own permissions)
    deactivate TS
    HTTP --> MCP : response
    deactivate HTTP
    MCP --> MW : tool result
    deactivate MCP
    MW -> MW : reset contextvars (finally)
    MW --> Client : MCP tool result
    deactivate MW
end

note over MW, TS : The client's token never touches disk and is scoped to one request:\nset in contextvars on the way in, reset in a finally on the way out.\nThe server holds <b>no</b> secret — Teamscale validates the forwarded credentials.

@enduml
